---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Is it available now?',
    a: "Not yet. We're building it and plan to open a small beta soon. Joining the waitlist is free, and we'll write to you when spots open.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Is this a SOC 2 report?',
    a: "No. SOC 2 is an audit by an independent CPA firm. Security Unblocker helps you answer buyers' security questions honestly today and organizes what an auditor will ask for later. It doesn't replace an audit, and it isn't legal advice.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Will enterprise buyers accept this instead of SOC 2?',
    a: "It depends on the buyer and the deal. Many early-stage pilots move forward when a vendor shows a clear, documented and honest security posture backed by evidence. Some buyers will still require a SOC 2 report, and nothing here changes that.",
  },
  {
    q: 'How is it different from a compliance platform?',
    a: "Compliance platforms are built around earning an audit, which is the right goal once you're ready for one. This is built for the earlier moment: one deal is waiting on a questionnaire, and you need accurate answers and a security packet this week. What it collects along the way is organized so it counts toward a later audit.",
  },
  {
    q: "What if a question asks for something we don't do?",
    a: "The plan is for the draft to say so. It states the gap plainly and suggests a realistic fix and date, instead of inventing an answer. You review and approve every answer before anything goes to a buyer.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Which questionnaire formats will it handle?',
    a: "We plan to support common formats such as SIG and CAIQ, plus custom Excel and CSV workbooks. Tell us what you're stuck on when you join the waitlist and we'll build for that first.",
  },
  {
    q: 'What will it be able to see in our accounts?',
    a: "Our design goal is read-only access to configuration settings, such as whether code review is required or storage is encrypted, and not your customers' data. Before anyone connects an account, we'll publish exactly what is read and why.",
  },
];
---
<section id="faq" class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="container section-pad">
    <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
    <h2 id="faq-title" class="h2">What founders ask first.</h2>

    <div class="list">
      {faqs.map((item) => (
        <details name="faq">
          <summary>
            <span>{item.q}</span>
            <svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path d="M5 8 L10 13 L15 8" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p>{item.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .h2 { margin-bottom: 40px; max-width: 760px; }

  .list {
    max-width: 820px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  details {
    background: var(--color-ground);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
  }

  summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    min-height: 60px;
    padding: 14px 24px;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.3;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }

  .chev {
    flex: none;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  details[open] .chev { transform: rotate(180deg); color: var(--color-accent); }

  details p {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 24px 22px;
    max-width: 68ch;
    color: var(--color-body);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .chev { transition: none; }
  }
</style>
